findings.problem:
The paper omits a directly overlapping earlier public candidate Lean statement: Rémondière's ClayYM v1.1.0, deposited on Zenodo on 2026-10-25. That statement already contains these elements, which this paper presents as its own contributions:
- a Wilson-lattice-limit variant;
- OS axioms;
- field content consisting of the 21 components of Tr F_{μν}F_{ρσ};
- a short-distance 'Yang–Mills fingerprint' ⟨θθ⟩ ~ κ/(x⁸ log² x), with the −b1/b0² correction and the same Caswell and Jones references;
- a mass gap that covers only the C-even sector (its Limitation 3, which matches row 1 of this paper's Table 2);
- Claude-written code and adversarial review by Claude agents.
The paper's survey sentence leaves the reader thinking the only public candidate statement is lean-dojo's. The abstract and Contributions then claim the 21-component clause and the 'asymptotic-freedom fingerprint' without crediting the earlier work. The author's own library had already found and verified this prior work.

